part.text:
Fixed. The issue was in `applyInverseRelationToCollection` (src/Illuminate/Database/Eloquent/Relations/Concerns/SupportsInverseRelations.php:97): the `chaperone()` `afterQuery` callback fires for every query execution on the relation, including `pluck()`, which returns a base collection of scalar values (e.g. integer IDs). Passing those scalars to the type-hinted `applyInverseRelationToModel(Model $model, ...)` threw a TypeError.

The fix skips non-`Model` items when applying the inverse relation, matching the test `testOnlyHydratesInverseRelationOnModels`:

```php
foreach ($models as $model) {
    if ($model instanceof Model) {
        $this->applyInverseRelationToModel($model, $parent);
    }
}
```

I also removed the debug instrumentation that had accumulated in that method and the now-unused imports. Verification:
- All 5 inverse-relation test files pass (67 tests, 439 assertions), including `testOnlyHydratesInverseRelationOnModels` which previously failed.
- Eloquent integration/builder/collection/model/relationship suites show the same result with and without the patch (4 pre-existing failures unrelated to this change).
